## 3. Phase 1: Wazuh Manager Deployment & Configuration (Ubuntu)

### Step 1: Network Verification and Server IP Address

* **Procedure / Commands:**
  ```bash
  ifconfig

Technical Explanation: Identification of active network interface (wlp2s0) and assigned IP (192.168.5.143). Configures listening ports for event ingestion (1514/1515 TCP/UDP) and Web HTTPS access (443).

Screenshot: ![Network Verification](img/01_ubuntu_network_configuration.png)

Control Alignment: ISO/IEC 27001:2022 A.8.20 (Network security) | CIS Controls 4 (Secure Configuration)

Step 2: Importing the Wazuh Repository GPG Key
Procedure / Commands:
curl -s [https://packages.wazuh.com/key/GPG-KEY-WAZUH](https://packages.wazuh.com/key/GPG-KEY-WAZUH) | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/wazuh-archive-keyring.gpg

Technical Explanation: Cryptographic signature verification. The GPG key ensures binary authenticity and prevents supply-chain or MitM tampering during package installation.

Screenshot: ![GPG Key Import](img/02_wazuh_gpg_key_import.png)
|Control Alignment: ISO/IEC 27001:2022 A.8.24 (Cryptography) | NIST SP 800-53 SI-7 (Software Integrity)

