Step 7: Manually Registering the Windows Agent on Manager (CLI)
Procedure / Commands:

Bash
sudo /var/ossec/bin/manage_agents
Select A (Add agent) → Name: WindowsHost → IP: 192.168.5.74 → Confirm: y

Technical Explanation: Enrolls endpoint into local database (client.keys). Binds IP address to agent ID: 001 to mitigate IP spoofing attacks.

Screenshot: ![CLI Agent Registration](img/07_wazuh_cli_add_agent.png)

Control Alignment: ISO/IEC 27001:2022 A.8.8 (Vulnerability & Asset Mgmt) | CIS Controls 1 (Asset Inventory)

Step 8: Extracting the Cryptographic Authentication Key
Procedure / Commands:

Bash
sudo /var/ossec/bin/manage_agents
Select E (Extract key) → Agent ID: 001

Technical Explanation: Exports Base64 pre-shared key (PSK). Enables mutual authentication and AES/Blowfish channel encryption between host and manager.

Screenshot: ![Key Extraction](img/08_wazuh_cli_extract_agent_key.png)

Control Alignment: ISO/IEC 27001:2022 A.8.24 (Key Management) | NIST SP 800-53 SC-12 (Cryptographic Key Establishment)

